# ksch.py self-test: exercises every symbol type, both label kinds, the router,
# junction detection and DNP dashing. `ksch.py check` on this file must print
# no ERROR lines and no overlap/crossing WARNs.
title ksch self-test
ic U1 14,2 REG p=3 L:1=EN,2=FB R:6=OUT T:5=VIN B:8=GND
pwr +5V U1.5
gnd U1.8
r R1 4,3 v 100k
r R2 4,9 v 33k
c C1 12,-2 v 1uF
pwr +5V R1.1
gnd R2.2
gnd C1.2
pwr +5V C1.1
wire R1.2 R2.1
wire R1.2 7,5 U1.1
label VOUT U1.6
nc U1.2
# discharge leg: FET, diode, inductor, and a DNP part
nmos Q1 4,20 r BSS138
r R3 0,20 h 10k
gnd Q1.s
gnd R3.1
wire R3.2 Q1.g
l L1 14,20 h 4.7uH
d D1 20,18 vr BAT54
c C2 24,18 v 10uF dnp
wire Q1.d L1.1
wire L1.2 D1.k
wire D1.k C2.1
gnd C2.2
hlabel SW_OUT D1.a out
# passives gallery, wired into one trunk so nothing is left dangling
fb FB1 30,4 v 600R
fuse F1 34,4 v 2A
tvs D2 38,4 v SMAJ5.0
sw SW1 42,4 v RESET
xtal Y1 46,4 v 32k768
tp TP1 50,4
net RAIL @y=2 FB1.1 F1.1 D2.1 SW1.1 Y1.1 TP1.1
net RTN @y=8 FB1.2 F1.2 D2.2 SW1.2 Y1.2
note 30,12 "gallery: every two-pin symbol on one trunk"
# dual diode (COM left), NTC, Kelvin shunt (sense right), flipped pwr/gnd glyphs
d2s D3 56,4 v BAT54S schottky
ntc TH1 60,4 v 10k
rsense R5 64,4 v 5m
net TOP @y=2 D3.1 TH1.1 R5.1
net BOT @y=10 D3.2 TH1.2
label COM D3.com
label SP R5.2
label SN R5.3
c C3 70,4 v 1uF
gnd C3.1
pwr -BATT C3.2
pwr -BATT R5.4
# row-collision cases knet's draw hit: a rotated cell's + vs its ref, a sideways gnd
# row over a sideways pwr row in one column, a named gnd off a left-facing pin, and a
# flat box one row under a long value
bat BT1 80,4 hr "21700 Li-ion"
r R6 80,7 hr 10k
d D4 80,10 hr PZU12B2L
conn U2 76,12 TPS259474LRPWR flat R:5=IN_5
gnd BT1.2 -BATT
pwr +3V3 R6.2
gnd D4.2 -BATT
net TRK @x=82 BT1.1 R6.1 D4.1 U2.5
